# heroes-js environment defaults. Copy to `.env` to override locally.
#
# NODE_ENV=development makes the local/dev environment explicit instead of
# relying on Express's implicit "development" default when this is unset.
# The deployed Docker image sets NODE_ENV=production itself (see
# docker/Dockerfile) -- don't set it to "production" here, that would
# suppress server/auth.ts's devCode convenience field for local login.
NODE_ENV=development
#
# LAN_HOST=1 binds the API to 0.0.0.0 so other machines on your network
# can join. Leave at 0 for single-machine dev (default).
LAN_HOST=0
#
# --- Postgres -------------------------------------------------------------
#
# server/persistence/db.ts reads these; the defaults below match
# docker-compose.yml's local `db` service, so leaving them unset uses your
# own container.
#
# To develop against the shared gameserver instead, point PGHOST at
# tufton-harvester's tailnet address (Tailscale must be up). This is the
# `.env`-only change described in
# plan/2026-08-09-architecture-walkthrough-tailscale.md -- no code edits.
#
#   PGHOST=100.68.178.28
#
# Two things to know before you do:
#   1. Tests deliberately ignore this. `npm test` / `npm run test:cityview`
#      load .env.test after .env, which pins Postgres back to 127.0.0.1 --
#      test/smoke.ts deletes every game in the database except its own
#      fixtures, which would destroy real saves on the gameserver.
#   2. Sharing the DB does not share the dev Network Map. Presence is an
#      in-memory registry per API process (server/telemetry/presenceRegistry.ts),
#      so the map only shows clients hitting *your* API. To watch the
#      gameserver's own players, point the client at its API instead:
#      API_HOST=100.68.178.28 with API_PORT=3001.
PGHOST=localhost
PGPORT=5432
PGUSER=gameuser
PGPASSWORD=gamepass
PGDATABASE=game_poc
